pi_j: the X-adjusted contrast of the Mills ratio lambda_j, top - bottom, in group j (the same
regression as C_j with lambda_j for y).
Std. err.: influence function of the whole procedure (probit, boundaries of the strata, regressions).
Reading: with kappa > 0 the gap falls across the strata (the eager treated at low P gain
more, the reluctant untreated at high P would have gained less); the signs of C1 and C0 need
only A2; kappa_dd uses the Mills ratios of A1. Never split on the outcome itself (collider).

